                    %a{:href => "#separable_closure"} Separable closure
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#galois_theory_for_separable_algebras"} Galois theory for separable algebras
              %li
                %a{:href => "#GaloisTheoryForSchemes"} Galois theory for schemes
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#StatementOfMainTheorem"} Statement of the main theorem
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#reproducing_classical_galois_theory_of_field_extensions"} Reproducing classical Galois theory of field extensions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#grothendiecks_galois_theory"} Grothendieck’s Galois Theory
              %li
                %a{:href => "#GaloisInTopos"} Galois theory in topos theory
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#reformulation_of_classical_galois_theory"} Reformulation of classical Galois theory
                %ul
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#observation"} Observation
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#topostheoretic_galois_theory"} Topos-theoretic Galois theory
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#higher_topos_theoretic_galois_theory"} Higher topos theoretic Galois theory
              %li
                %a{:href => "#la_longue_marche__travers_la_thorie_de_galois"} ‘La Longue Marche à travers la Théorie de Galois’
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_entries"} Related entries
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Classical Galois theory classifies
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+extensions"} field extensions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+sheaves"} locally constant sheaves
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representations"} permutation representations
            of the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
          %p
            Even more generally one can define a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+group"} Galois group
            associated to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable (infinity,1)-category
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Mathew14"} Mathew 14
          %h2#ClassicalGaloisTheory Classical Galois theory for fields
          %p
            We discuss the classical/traditional case of Galois theory, which concerns the classification of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+extensions"} field extensions
            %em
              %a{:href => "#GaloisTheoryForSchemes"} Galois theory for schemes
            and then in
            %em
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Galois+theory#GaloisInTopos"} Galois theory in a topos
            we discuss how this is a special case of a more general concept of Galois theory in a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
          %h3#GaloisTheoryForFields Galois theory of fields
          #GaloisExtension.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              We call a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+extension"} field extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset L
              a
              %strong Galois extension
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset L
              is algebraic and there exists a subgroup
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \subset Aut(L)
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \simeq L^G
              is the field of elements that are invariant under
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          #GaloisGroup.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset L
              is a Galois extension, we define the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+group"} Galois group
              to be
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gal
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Aut
                      %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Gal(L/K) := Aut_K(L)
                    \\,.
          %p This means that we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mrow
                      %mi Gal
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K \simeq L^{Gal(L/K)}
                  \\,.
          #separable.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar K
              be a fixed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+closure"} algebraic closure
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \subset K[X] - \{0\}
              is any collection of non-zero
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/splitting+field"} splitting field
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfield"} subfield
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar K
              generated by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              and the zeros of the polynomials in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %p
              We call
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in K[X]- \{0\}
              %strong separable
              if it has no multiple zero in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar K
            %p
              We call
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in \bar K
              %strong
                separable over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+polynomial"} irreducible polynomial
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi f
                      %mi K
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\alpha_K
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is separable.
            %p
              A subextension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \subset \bar K
              is called
              %strong
                separable over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              if each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in L
              is separable over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          #normal.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              We call
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              %strong normal
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              if for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \in L
              the polynomial
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi f
                      %mi K
                      %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\alpha_K
              splits completely in linear factors in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L[X]
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfield"} subfield
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar K
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K \subset L \subset \bar K
                    \\,.
            %p
              Denote by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfields"} subfields
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              for which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is a finite Galois extension of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} partially ordered
              by inclusion is a directed poset.
            %p The following assertions are equivalent:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                  is a
                  %a{:href => "#GaloisExtension"} Galois extension
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                  is
                  %a{:href => "#normal"} normal
                  and
                  %a{:href => "#separable"} separable
                  over
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %li
                %p
                  There is a set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \subset K[X] - \{0\}
                  of separable polynomials such that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                  is the
                  %a{:href => "#separable"} splitting field
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  over
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                          %mrow
                            %mi E
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi I
                        %mi E
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{E \in I} E \simeq L
            %p
              If these conditions are satisfied, then there is a group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gal
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mi Gal
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Gal(L/K) \simeq {\lim_{\leftarrow}}_{E \in I} Gal(E/K)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the right we have the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfield"} subfield
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contravariant+functor"} contravariant functor
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ↦
                      %mi Gal
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \mapsto Gal(E/K)
          %p
            Since each group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gal
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gal(E/K)
            is finite, the above isomorphism can be used to equip
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gal
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gal(L/K)
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+space"} profinite topology
            (i.e. take the limit in the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+groups"} topological groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gal
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gal(E/K)
            has the discrete topology), making it into a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+group"} profinite group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gal
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gal(L/K)
            as a profinite group in this way.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/main+theorem+of+classical+Galois+theory"}> main theorem of classical Galois theory
              )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset L
              be a
              %a{:href => "#GaloisExtension"} Galois extension
              of fields with
              %a{:href => "#GaloisGroup"} Galois group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset L
              correspond bijectively to the closed subgroups of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %p More precisely, the maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi E
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi is
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi subfield
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi of
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi L
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi containing
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ←
                        %mi ψ
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi H
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi is
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi closed
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi subgroup
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi of
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{E | E\;is\;a\;subfield\;of\;L\;containing\;K\}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{\phi}{\to}}{\underset{\psi}{\leftarrow}}
                    \\{H|H\;is\;a\;closed\;subgroup\;of\;G\}
            %p defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Aut
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi(E) = Aut_E(L)
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\psi(H) = L^H
            %p
              are bijective and inverse to each other. This correspondence reverses the inclusion relation:
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              corresponds to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi id
                        %mi L
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{id_L\}
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              corresponds to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset E
                  is finite precisely if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                  is open (in the profinite topology on
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi E
                        %mo :
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi index
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi G
                        %mo :
                        %mi H
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [E:K] \simeq index[G:H]
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                  is open;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \subset L
                  is Galois with
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Gal
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi L
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gal(L/E) \simeq H
                  (as
                  = succeed "s);" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              %li
                %p
                  for every
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma \in G
                  we have that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma[E]
                  corresponds to
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                          %mi H
                          %msup
                            %mi σ
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma H \sigma^{-1}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset E
                  is Galois precisely if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
                  is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+subgroup"} normal subgroup
                  of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Gal
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gal(E/K) \simeq G/H
                  (as
                  = succeed "s)" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset E
                  is Galois.
          %p
            This appears for instance as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Lenstra"} Lenstra, theorem 2.3
          %p
            This suggests that more fundamental than the subgroups of a Galois group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            are its quotients by subgroups, which can be identified with transitive
            = succeed "-sets." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-sets." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %h3#in_terms_of_separable_algebras In terms of separable algebras
          %h4#free_modules Free modules
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            A collection of elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (w_i)_{i \in I}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            (over
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in N
            there is a unique collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_i)_{i \in I}
            of elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_i = 0
            for all but finitely many
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = \sum_{i \in I} a_i w_i
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            has a basis it is called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free
            (over
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is free with basis a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is
            %em
              free with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            (over
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated"} finitely generated
            free module.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            be a finitely generated free
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_1, w_2, \cdots, w_n
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi N
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon N \to N
            be
            = succeed "-linear." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi j
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi j
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi i
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f(w_i) = \sum_{j = 1}^n a_{i j} w_j \;\;\;
                  (1 \leq i \leq n)
          %p
            for certain
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{i j} \in A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tr(f)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi i
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Tr(f) = \sum_{i = 1}^n a_{i i}
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is an element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            that only depends on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tr
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi N
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tr : Hom_A(N,N) \to A
            is
            = succeed "-linear." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h4#separable_algebras Separable algebras
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is free with finite rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            as an
            = succeed "-module." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
            the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi mult
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} mult_b\colon B \to B
            defined by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi mult
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi b
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} mult_b\colon x \mapsto b x
            is
            = succeed "-linear," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tr(b)
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Tr
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tr_{B/A}(b)
            is defined to be
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Tr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi mult
                      %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tr(mult_b)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tr
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tr\colon B \to A
            is easily seen to be
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi n
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tr(a) = n a
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_A(B,A)
            (underlying which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with the same rank as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi\colon B \to Hom_A(B,A)
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi y
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi Tr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi(x) : y \mapsto Tr(x y)
                  \\,,
          %p
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in B
          #SeparableAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              If for an
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              the the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              we call
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              = succeed "," do
                %strong
                  separable over
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %strong
                free separable
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              if we wish to stress the condition that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is finitely generated and free as an
              = succeed "-module." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h4#separable_closure Separable closure
          %p
            Recall the notion of
            %a{:href => "#separable"} separable elements
          #SeparableClosure.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar K
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+closure"} algebraic closure
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+closure"} separable closure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_S
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi S
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi is
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi separable
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi over
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K_S \simeq \{x \in \bar K | x \; is \; separable \; over \; K\}
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              We have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_S
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subfield"} subfield
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar K
              and that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi S
                    %mo ≃
                    %mover
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_S \simeq \bar K
              precisely if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+field"} perfect field
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              is 0.
            %p
              From xyz it follows that the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \subset K_S
              is Galois.
          #AbsoluteGaloisGroup.num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              The Galois group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gal
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gal(K_S/K)
              is called the
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+Galois+group"} absolute Galois group
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %h4#galois_theory_for_separable_algebras Galois theory for separable algebras
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_3 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(Spec K)
              its
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#AbsoluteGaloisGroup"} absolute Galois group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi SAlg
                      %mi K
                      %mi op
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Set
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SAlg_K^{op} \simeq \pi_1(Spec K) Set
                    \\,.
          %h2#GaloisTheoryForSchemes Galois theory for schemes
          %p
            The classical Galois theory for fields is a special case of a general geometric/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theoretic
            statement about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+sheaves"} locally constant sheaves
            and the action of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
            on their
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
          %h3#StatementOfMainTheorem Statement of the main theorem
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
              %strong
                finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphism"} étale morphism
              if there exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subset"} open subset
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mi Spec
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i = Spec A_i
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  the open subschemes
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(U_i)
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                  is affine,
              %li
                %p
                  and equal to
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Spec
                          %msub
                            %mi B
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec B_i
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi B
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_i
                  is a free
                  %a{:href => "#SeparableAlgebra"} separable
                  = succeed "-algebra." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_i
            %p
              In this situation we also say that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f  : Y \to X
              is a
              %strong finite étale covering
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              from a finite étale covering
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
              to a finite étale covering
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi Z
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : Z \to X
              is a morphism of schemes
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h : Y \to Z
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo =
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi h
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = g \circ h
            %p
              This defines the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi FEt
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FEt_X
              of finite étale covers of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          #TheoremGaloisTheoryForSchemes.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_4 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected"} connected
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+group"} profinite group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
              – the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group"} fundamental group
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              – uniquely determined up to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %a{:href => "#FiniteEtMorphisms"} category of finite étale coverings
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FEex
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FEex
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fin
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fin \pi_1(X) Set
              of finite
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation+representation"} permutation representation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"}> finite set
              s, with the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topology"} discrete topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
              acts continuously).
          %p
            This appears for instance as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Lenstra"} Lenstra, main theorem 1.11
            = succeed "1." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA"} SGA
          %p
            The
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profinite+group"} profinite group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+fundamental+group"} étale fundamental group
            of the connected scheme
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA1"} SGA1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
            depends on the choice of a
            %em fibre functor
            given by a geometric point of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "-torsor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck%27s+section+conjecture"} Grothendieck's section conjecture
          .num_example
            %h6#examples Examples
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  copies of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  corresponds, under this theorem, to a finite set of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  elements on which
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
                  acts trivially.
              %li
                %p
                  The fact that for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo =
                        %mi Spec
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = Spec \mathbb{Z}
                  there are no other finite étale coverings of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  is thus expressed by the group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Spec
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(Spec \mathbb{Z})
                  being
                  %em trivial
                  \.
              %li
                %p
                  The same is true for
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Spec
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(Spec K)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  is an
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed field
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  is an arbitrary
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Spec
                        %mi K
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(Spec K)
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+Galois+group"} absolute Galois group
                  of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+group"} Galois group
                  of the
                  %a{:href => "#SeparableClosure"} separable closure
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi K
                          %mi S
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_S
                  over
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheoremGaloisTheoryForSchemes"}
                  is a reformulation of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "#ClassicalGaloisTheory"} classical Galois theory
              %li
                %p
                  In particular, if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  is a finite field, then
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Spec
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≃
                          %mover
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(Spec K) \simeq \hat \mathbb{Z}
              %li
                %p
                  Let
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo =
                          %mi Spec
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = Spec A
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+of+integers"} ring of integers
                  in an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+number+field"} algebraic number field
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                  be the maximal
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+extension"} algebraic extension
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                  that is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unramified"} unramified
                  at all non-zero prime ideals of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
                  is the Galois group of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                  over
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %li
                %p
                  More generally, if
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ≠
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \neq 0
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Spec
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(Spec A[\frac{1}{a}])
                  is the Galois group, over
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                  that is unramified at all non-zero prime ideals of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  not dividing
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
          %h3#reproducing_classical_galois_theory_of_field_extensions Reproducing classical Galois theory of field extensions
          %p
            In this section we explain the connection between the main theorem of Galois theory for schemes, theorem
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheoremGaloisTheoryForSchemes"}
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ClassicalGaloisTheory"} classical Galois theory
          %p
            We denote by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            of the category of free separable
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            = succeed "-sets," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheoremGaloisTheoryForSchemes"}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = Spec K
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
            is trivial, so that the category of finite
            = succeed "-sets" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1(X)
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_5 Theorem
            %p (…)
          %h2#grothendiecks_galois_theory Grothendieck’s Galois Theory
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA1"} SGA1
            = succeed "." do
              %em Galois categories
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %em fibre functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi FinSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: \mathcal{C}\to FinSet
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck%27s+Galois+theory"} Grothendieck's Galois theory
          %h2#GaloisInTopos Galois theory in topos theory
          %p
            One notices that
            %a{:href => "#ClassicalGaloisTheory"} classical Galois theory
            has an equivalent reformulation in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
          %h3#reformulation_of_classical_galois_theory Reformulation of classical Galois theory
          .num_prop
            %h6#observation Observation
            %p
              The
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphism"} étale morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Y \to X
              corresponds precisely to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+sheaves"} locally constant sheaves
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with respect to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+topology"} étale topology
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+cover"} étale cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+sheaf"} constant sheaf
              on each
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Et(K)
              be its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+site"} small
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{E} := Sh(Et(K))
            %p
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              over it. This topos is a
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"}> local topos
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"}> locally connected topos
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topos"}> connected topos
                  \.
            %p
              Then Galois extensions of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              correspond precisely to the
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+object"} locally constant object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              on them is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+topos"} Galois topos
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Gal
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gal(\mathcal{E}) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{E}
            %p
              The Galois group is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group+of+a+topos"} fundamental group of the topos
          %h3#topostheoretic_galois_theory Topos-theoretic Galois theory
          %p
            Accordingly in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            Galois theory is generally about the classification of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+sheaves"} locally constant sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group+of+a+topos"} fundamental group of the topos
            \.
          %p (…)
          %h3#higher_topos_theoretic_galois_theory Higher topos theoretic Galois theory
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+topos+theory"} higher topos theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} shape theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            has an associated fundamental ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(\mathbf{H})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-space"} pro-space
            whose
            = succeed "-truncation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(\mathbf{H})
            is the ordinary fundamental groupoid of the underlying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-topos"} 1-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(\mathbf{H})
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_1(\mathbf{H})\to Set
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_6 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+n-connected+%28n%2B1%2C1%29-topos"} locally n-connected (n+1,1)-topos
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -1\leq n\leq \infty
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi lc
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Fun
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{H}^lc \simeq \Fun(\Pi_{n+1}(\mathbf{H}), n Grpd),
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi lc
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}^{lc}\subset\mathbf{H}
              is the subcategory of locally constant objects.
          %p
            This generalization of Galois theory is discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#Grothendieck75"}> Grothendieck 75
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Hoyois13"} Hoyois 13
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Hoyois15"} Hoyois 15
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=\infty
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+--+structures"}> cohesive (infinity,1)-topos – structures
              –
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/cohesive+%28infinity,1%29-topos+--+structures#GaloisTheory"} Galois theory
          %h2#la_longue_marche__travers_la_thorie_de_galois ‘La Longue Marche à travers la Théorie de Galois’
          %p
            Between January and June 1981, Grothendieck wrote about 1600 manuscript pages of a work with the above title. The subject is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AbsoluteGaloisGroup"} absolute Galois group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gal
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gal(\overline{\mathbb{Q}},\mathbb{Q})
            of the rational numbers and its
            %strong geometric
            action on moduli spaces of Riemann surfaces. This will (one day be) discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Long+March"} Long March
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anabelian+geometry"} anabelian geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/children%27s+drawings"} children's drawings
            (in other words
            = succeed "," do
              %em Dessins d’enfants
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck-Teichmuller+group"} Grothendieck-Teichmuller group
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anabelian+geometry"} anabelian
            question is:
            %em
              how much information about the isomorphism class of an algebraic variety,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is contained in the étale fundamental group of
              = succeed "?" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            Grothendieck calls varieties which are completely determined by their
            = succeed "," do
              %strong étale fundamental group
            = succeed "." do
              %em anabelian varieties
          %p (…)
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+group"}> Galois group
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+Galois+group"} motivic Galois group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+connection"} Galois connection
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+Galois+theory"}> categorical Galois theory
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck%27s+Galois+theory"} Grothendieck's Galois theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+cover"} Galois cover
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+Galois+theory"} differential Galois theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+cohomology"} Galois cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lascar+group"} Lascar group
                (a Galois group of first order theories)
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+covering+spaces"} fundamental theorem of covering spaces
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anabelian+geometry"} anabelian geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+groups+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"}> geometric homotopy groups in an (∞,1)-topos
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group+of+a+topos"} fundamental group of a topos
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} fundamental ∞-groupoid of an (∞,1)-topos
          %h2#references References
          %p Original articles:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Abstract Galois Theory
                %strong 19
                (1980) 21–42 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.mcgill.ca/barr/papers/galois.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Barr-AbstractGaloisI.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Abstract Galois Theory II
                %strong 25
                3 (1982) 227–247 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(82)90080-9"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(82)90080-9
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.mcgill.ca/barr/papers/galois2.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Barr-AbstractGaloisII.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Introduction:
          %ul
            %li#Lenstra
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hendrik+Lenstra"}> Hendrik Lenstra
                ,
                %em Galois theory for schemes
                , Mathematisch Instituut Universiteit van Amsterdam (1985) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://websites.math.leidenuniv.nl/algebra/GSchemes.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p Some of the material above is taken from this.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ravi+Vakil"}> Ravi Vakil
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kirsten+Wickelgren"} Kirsten Wickelgren
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Universal covering spaces and fundamental groups in algebraic geometry as schemes
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.stanford.edu/~vakil/files/VW2Dec1910.pdf"} pdf
          %p Monographs:
          %ul
            %li#BorceuxJanelidze2001
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Janelidze"} George Janelidze
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Galois+Theories"} Galois Theories
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Pierre+Tignol"}> Jean-Pierre Tignol
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Galois’ Theory of Algebraic Equations
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/4628"} doi:10.1142/4628
          %p The locally simply connected case is discussed for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              Marco Robalo,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Galois theory towards dessins d’enfants
              %a{:href => "https://dspace.ist.utl.pt/bitstream/2295/575330/1/dissertacao.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Galois theory in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} stable (infinity,1)-category
            is developed in
          %ul#Mathew14
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akhil+Mathew"}> Akhil Mathew
              , The Galois group of a stable homotopy theory,
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1404.2156"} arXiv
          %p Galois theory in (higher) topos theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA4"}> SGA4
                ,
                %em Expose VIII, Proposition 2.1.
            %li#Hoyois15
